---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Editorial policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: sources, fixes`} description="Which official guides and government pages Citizenship Test Free relies on, how its practice questions are written, which sources it refuses and how a mistake is corrected and dated." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial and corrections policy</h1>
    <p>People use these pages to decide when to apply for citizenship and to pay for a test. A stale fee or a wrong day limit can cost them a refused application, so every figure points back to the official page it was read on.</p>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>{AUTHOR_NAME}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we read</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>gov.uk and the Home Office: the Life in the UK Test pages, the naturalisation guidance and the fees table;</li>
      <li>the Australian Department of Home Affairs: the test pages, the residence requirement, form 1298i and processing times, and Our Common Bond;</li>
      <li>Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada: the test and study pages, eligibility, the physical presence instructions, the fee list and Discover Canada.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How the questions are written</h2><p>We write every question from a fact in the official guide of the country. We never copy a question from an app, a book, another practice site or a real test, and we never present our questions as the official ones.</p>
    <h2>Sources we refuse</h2><p>Law firms, migration agents, app publishers and practice sites never supply a figure here. A rule we cannot find on an official page is not published.</p>
    <h2>Review cycle</h2><p>A script compares the official fee tables and processing times with our parameter file every month. The guides and rules are re-read when a government announces a change, and the UK earned settlement reform is followed until its rules are final. Every page shows the date of the last check.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <ol><li>We open the official page again.</li><li>We correct the parameter file or the question and add a test for the case.</li><li>The site rebuilds and shows the new date.</li></ol>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No law firm, adviser, publisher or government pays for or reviews what is published here, and the site carries no affiliate link. See also the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>. Version: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
